          "title": "You'll want to know: mōnstrum, mōnstrī",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "mōnstrum, mōnstrī — \"a monster; a portent\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Mōnstrum ingēns in spēluncā habitābat. A huge monster lived in the cave."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Neuter, from moneō, 'to warn': first a sign sent by the gods, then a monster. English monster."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "mōnstrum is built on moneō, \"to warn\" (EtymDB, Lewis & Short): a warning sign, a portent, and then a monster. English monster comes from it through French."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
